id: pm-rl-7c7m
title: Stabilize packed LM CLI timing under the unchanged acceptance bound
description: "The full release gate observed an existing packed LM CLI timing failure: measured CLI 22138 ms against its unchanged 20000 ms bound. The same unmodified test passed alone at 8955 ms. Investigate repeatable runtime and IO overhead under full coverage without hiding source or weakening the acceptance bound."
type: Task
status: open
priority: 3
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-15T18:17:46.948Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-26T22:36:48.400Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Repeated full npm and Bun gates satisfy the existing 20-second packed LM CLI acceptance on declared runner resources; coverage scope and all four thresholds remain unchanged; measurements distinguish CLI time from total test setup time.
parent: pm-rl-mjo5
comments[12]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-16T02:20:26.445Z",codex-agent,"Reused for the existing packed LM CLI timing failure during the Compose LM release gate. At f405171 the unchanged test reports failure after 28607.147 ms total test time; exact failure detail awaits the completed Node reporter footer, so this is not asserted to be the measured CLI duration. The previous complete df70cb0 test run passed this unchanged case at measured CLI 14697.724 ms and all 590 tests passed (that gate separately refused one statement block, now covered). No deadline, allowance or threshold was changed. The current attempt continues only to retain complete diagnostics; it is not gate approval. New real-container LM execution, staged recovery and cancellation already pass in this attempt."
  "2026-10-16T02:52:07.374Z",codex-agent,"Completed f405171 full npm diagnostics: 590 total, 589 pass, 1 fail, zero cancelled/skipped. The sole failure is measured real CLI 23890 ms versus unchanged 20000 ms. All new Compose LM cases pass; L/B/F are 100%; separate raw-counter diagnostic is 3979/3979 blocks across 30 authored sources. PM-linked direct command first fails before training because default schema PM_PATH redirects implicit SDK init to existing sandbox settings. Supported none context correctly requires snapshot/isolated workspace. With none plus snapshot the command reaches the real CLI and fails its unchanged 25000 ms child timeout. No timeout or threshold was weakened, no settings were forced, and no upstream PM changes or issues were filed. The context interaction and timing are separate observations."
  "2026-10-16T03:03:22.522Z",codex-agent,"Node 26.7 focused packed acceptance also reaches the unchanged 25000 ms child timeout, so changing to the existing CI runtime does not resolve the observed timing. Inspecting a bounded numerical optimization in an isolated source snapshot: memoize at most 128 next-token logit rows within one fixed-policy held-out evaluation, with a fresh cache for each policy/evaluation. Keep all episodes, softmax calculations, LCG draws, rewards and gate inputs identical. Plan a deterministic real-weight access-count regression against the uncached sampler plus exact seeded reward equality, including a behavioural revert. No main worktree source or threshold has changed yet."
  "2026-10-16T03:04:23.609Z",codex-agent,"The independent f405171 Bun gate now passes the unchanged packed CLI case at measured 9620.706 ms (17643.969 ms total test time), with the same canonical checkpoints and held-out rewards. This follows the 23890 ms full npm failure and the focused timeout observations, so uncontrolled timing variation remains evidenced. The bounded cache idea was inspected but no sampling source or tests were changed; the prepared prototype contains no implementation changes and is discarded. Keep the product source/test tree frozen while completing both literal gates in isolated validation checkouts. This does not claim the timing follow-up is fixed."
  "2026-10-16T03:30:46.801Z",codex-agent,"The full literal Bun release gate at f405171 completes exit 0: all 590 tests pass, zero skips, every coverage dimension 100% over 30 sources, plus audit/pack/changelog. Its unchanged packed LM CLI measured 9620.706 ms. This successful run does not remove the retained 23890 ms npm failure or focused timeouts; timing variability remains an open follow-up. No sampling optimization or threshold change was applied."
  "2026-10-16T03:47:20.390Z",codex-agent,"Final same-source isolated literal npm release gate passes 590/590 with zero skips and all four coverage dimensions 100%; packed LM CLI measured 11716.141 ms. Literal Bun also passes 590/590 and measured 9620.706 ms. Retain the observed 23890 ms failed attempt and focused timeouts as evidence of unresolved timing variability; no sampling optimization or threshold change was applied. PM test UX observations are separate: default schema PM_PATH collides with this fixture implicit init; none requires snapshot/isolated workspace, and none plus snapshot reaches the benchmark. Automatic result tracking is disabled, so results are recorded in comments. No upstream PM repository changes or issues were filed. Return this existing follow-up to open, without claiming its timing stability criterion solved."
  "2026-10-16T04:19:45.627Z",codex-agent,"Review round 1: addressing the linked command failure under the normal PM test context. Will preserve append-only history and use pinned pm test remove/add, then run the linked acceptance through pm test without weakening its CLI timing assertion."
  "2026-10-16T04:22:42.537Z",codex-agent,"Revert proof: the original linked command under default schema context fails before training with init_existing_settings_requires_force. With only fixture init changed to pass its own explicit temporary pmRoot, the same normal pm test invocation reaches the unchanged CLI timing assertion: observed 22003 ms exceeds 20000 ms in this attempt. Pinned pm test remove/add replaced the link without editing existing history. Context collision is fixed; timing variability remains separate and the item stays active."
  "2026-10-16T04:36:55.887Z",codex-agent,"Further normal-schema linked runs reach training: observed CLI 23191 ms against the unchanged 20000 ms assertion, and a separate Node 26 attempt reaches the existing 25000 ms child timeout. Isolated HOME does not remove that timing variability on this host. These are benchmark failures, not fixture-init collisions; retain them without calling timing stability fixed. Automatic PM test-result recording remains disabled, so explicit comments retain the results."
  "2026-10-16T05:51:25.100Z",codex-agent,"The linked command now passes normally through pinned pm test pm-rl-7c7m --run --progress on Node 26.12.0, default schema context and source workspace, exit 0 (1/1). It retains the 20000 ms CLI assertion and 25000 ms child timeout. Its total PM-run time is 28377 ms, which includes package setup and must not be called measured CLI time. The literal Bun gate separately measures CLI 11086.851 ms and passes all 590 tests. Retain prior assertion failures and timeout observations as timing-variability evidence; fixture initialization is fixed by explicit temporary pmRoot, without forced settings or PM context overrides. Old history is unchanged and the test link was replaced through pinned remove/add."
  "2026-10-16T06:12:46.388Z",codex-agent,"Final linked acceptance on exact CI Node 26.12.0 passes 1/1 through the normal pinned pm test --run --progress workflow: measured CLI 14597.809 ms, total linked-command time 28377 ms. Fixture initialization explicitly targets its own temporary pmRoot and does not require a PM context override or forced settings. Both final full literal gates pass 590/590 at unchanged thresholds; npm packed CLI measures 10996.891 ms and Bun 11086.851 ms. Retain earlier 22003/23191 ms assertion failures and 25000 ms child timeouts as unresolved timing variability rather than claiming stable performance. Return this timing follow-up to open; the linked-command context finding is fixed. Existing history is append-only and the original byte prefix was verified unchanged."
  "2026-10-26T22:36:48.400Z",codex-agent,"The current complete npm toolchain gate reports the packed three-generation LM CLI case failing after 37088.859383 ms against its unchanged 20-second acceptance bound. Reuse this existing timing item rather than create a duplicate. This is a separate local failure from the corrected unsupported hash options in lineage fixtures; no deadline, generation, contamination assertion or coverage threshold was changed. Detailed gate results are still pending."
